{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on the platform's own recorded distances, which is exactly the measure POL-RD-22 prescribes: trip_record.actual_distance_km of 24.8 less trip_record.optimal_distance_km of 20.5 is 4.30 km, more than four times POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance. POL-RD-22 expressly forbids re-measuring the route from the sparse trace, so the trace's low fix count cannot shrink this figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00902"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver never informed the rider of the deviation, as POL-RD-21 requires him to do by in-app chat before or at the point of deviation. None of the six chat entries announces a reroute or gives even a brief reason for one; the only messages sent while the trip ran are the rider's 13:24 query ('are we going the right way? This doesn't look like the usual route to the airport') and the driver's 13:25 reply 'Don't worry, I know the way. We will reach on time.', which explains nothing. Trip record's in_app_calls is empty, so no verbal notice can be established from the record (POL-GEN-26): the notice obligation is unmet and this is not an agreed deviation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00902", "EV-TRIP-00902"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The excess distance fare is fixed by POL-RD-24's formula at the base per-km rate and without surge: 4.30 km x 0.80 SGD/km = 3.44 SGD. The fare ledger reports the same per_km_rate_sgd of 0.80 and the same excess_distance_fare_sgd of 3.44, matching the policy's own excess_distance_fare threshold block. That 3.44 SGD is the sum the rider is owed for the deviation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00902", "EV-TRIP-00902"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Whichever open row of POL-RD-24's matrix applies, the rider is owed that 3.44 SGD in full: row (b) (traffic-justified but rider not informed) and row (d) (not traffic-justified) both pay the whole excess distance fare, so even accepting for argument that the PIE vehicle-fire advisory (EV-ADVIS-00902-01) satisfies POL-RD-23, that advisory can only move the case between rows (b) and (d) and cannot reduce the sum. Rows (a) and (c) are unavailable on this record: no notice was given, and 4.30 km is far outside the 1.0 km tolerance.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00902", "EV-TRIP-00902", "EV-CHAT-00902", "EV-ADVIS-00902-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only advisory anchored to the line the driver actually drove, the ECP one, does not justify a reroute under POL-RD-23: it does not intersect the recommended route and its type TRAFFIC_FLOW is not one of the kinds POL-RD-23 names (closure, congestion, incident). Whatever the driver believed about his alternative, his own route carries no admissible traffic justification of its own.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00902-03"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.derived.v7.justifies_reroute",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider is still carrying the charge. The ledger shows payment_status CHARGED, total_charged 35.00 and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so nothing has been returned to her. Under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION would leave that state standing and is not a rider-favourable outcome here; what the rider needs is a disposition that does not leave her bearing the disputed charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00902"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The AI cannot rule this case on its merits, and should not try: POL-RD-25 lets an AI ruling on a route deviation stand only where the deviation is 2 km or less, and this deviation is 4.30 km, so the case is escalated. That is the rider-protective disposition — under POL-GEN-03 an escalated case goes to a human reviewer, no monetary outcome issues and the contested amount is held rather than resolved against the rider — and it carries her 3.44 SGD excess-distance measure, and the balance of the 6.50 SGD she asks, to that reviewer instead of dismissing them.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00902"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-25", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.over_ai_limit",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The longer route was driven across the whole journey, not at its end: the trace's first fix is at 13:15:00 and its last at 13:52:00, the trip's own start and end, so the driver had the entire trip in which to give the POL-RD-21 notice and never did. The trace is IMPAIRED (issue LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, weight_multiplier 0.8) and I rely on its timestamps only; its geometry is not used to re-measure distance, exactly as POL-RD-22 directs.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00902"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.first_fix_at",
      "asserted_weight": 0.8
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither profile carries a fraud flag — rider 0 and driver 0 — so POL-GEN-22's 0.95 confidence uplift is not engaged, and the only obstacle between this record and an AI ruling is POL-RD-25's 2 km ceiling. The rider's claim is untarnished on the profile test that names this field and must not be dismissed on profile grounds.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00902", "EV-DPROF-00902"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.fraud_flags",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
